1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,240
Monday morning. Thirty students, forty minutes and one tricky concept.

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:13,440
What if your students could discover it themselves, while you guide them?

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:20,029
Welcome to the teacher’s side of İDÜ Lab.

4
00:00:28,775 --> 00:00:33,615
The teaching guide starts from one simple idea: one lesson, one game.

5
00:00:33,675 --> 00:00:39,715
A forty-minute lesson flow helps you plan the whole period.

6
00:00:39,775 --> 00:00:48,415
Games are aligned with the Türkiye Yüzyılı Maarif Modeli, and every world page lists its levels and key concepts.

7
00:00:48,475 --> 00:00:53,015
Students can play the first three levels without an account.

8
00:00:53,075 --> 00:00:58,673
And the science guides can be read and printed, even without JavaScript.

9
00:00:59,283 --> 00:01:00,923
In class, open a room.

10
00:01:00,983 --> 00:01:07,923
Teams join with a room code and a team name: no accounts and no personal data.

11
00:01:07,983 --> 00:01:15,923
No phones at school? Teams join from the computer lab, or the class plays in board mode.

12
00:01:15,983 --> 00:01:21,923
Everyone predicts, groups take turns, and the whole room sees the result.

13
00:01:21,983 --> 00:01:29,182
It’s loud, it’s fun, and it’s real science.

14
00:01:29,792 --> 00:01:36,932
Short on time? Open a ready-made lesson and go.

15
00:01:36,992 --> 00:01:43,232
School codes connect your students to your school.

16
00:01:43,292 --> 00:01:50,232
With Science Passport class assignments, the server checks each result in its own game engine.

17
00:01:50,292 --> 00:01:55,232
Achievements become signed Open Badges that anyone can verify.

18
00:01:55,292 --> 00:01:59,690
Evidence, not guesswork.

19
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:02,940
Is there a topic no game covers yet?

20
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,140
Request one, from anywhere in the world, without an account.

21
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:12,340
Describe the topic, the level and what your students should understand.

22
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:19,540
You get a tracking code; the team designs the game, tests it with you and publishes it.

23
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:30,198
Or build your school’s own game in Guest Studio: no code needed, reviewed by the university team, and published under your school’s name.

24
00:02:30,708 --> 00:02:32,048
Being a teacher at İDÜ Lab means this:

25
00:02:32,108 --> 00:02:34,048
You don’t hand out the answers.

26
00:02:34,108 --> 00:02:38,048
You guide the discovery.

27
00:02:38,108 --> 00:02:46,470
And your students own what they discover.

